--- /dev/null
+++ b/deploy/systemd/fsn-stats-proxy.service
@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+[Unit]
+Description=Fusion dashboard HTTPS proxy
+After=network.target
+StartLimitIntervalSec=60s
+StartLimitBurst=5
+
+[Service]
+Type=exec
+User=fsn-stats-proxy
+Group=fsn-stats-proxy
+RuntimeDirectory=fsn-stats-proxy
+RuntimeDirectoryMode=0700
+LogsDirectory=fsn-stats-proxy
+LogsDirectoryMode=0750
+ExecStartPre=/usr/sbin/nginx -t -q -e stderr -c /etc/fsn-stats/nginx.conf
+ExecStart=/usr/sbin/nginx -e stderr -c /etc/fsn-stats/nginx.conf
+ExecReload=/usr/sbin/nginx -t -q -e stderr -c /etc/fsn-stats/nginx.conf
+ExecReload=/bin/kill -HUP $MAINPID
+Restart=always
+RestartSec=5s
+KillSignal=SIGQUIT
+KillMode=mixed
+TimeoutStopSec=15s
+UMask=0027
+NoNewPrivileges=yes
+ProtectSystem=strict
+ProtectHome=yes
+PrivateTmp=yes
+PrivateDevices=yes
+RestrictSUIDSGID=yes
+RestrictAddressFamilies=AF_UNIX AF_INET AF_INET6
+CapabilityBoundingSet=CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE
+AmbientCapabilities=CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE
+LimitCORE=0
+StandardOutput=journal
+StandardError=journal
+LogNamespace=fsn-stats
+
+[Install]
+WantedBy=multi-user.target
diff --git a/docs/proxy-lifecycle.md b/docs/proxy-lifecycle.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..45545671e4a7f7536f1d429f26ad3dd634c15b2e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/proxy-lifecycle.md
@@ -0,0 +1,116 @@
+# Proxy supervision, logs and certificate replacement
+
+The candidate adds `fsn-stats-proxy.service`, `fsn-stats-logrotate.service` and
+`fsn-stats-logrotate.timer` under `deploy/systemd/`, plus `deploy/logrotate.conf`.
+The nginx template separates `@@RUN@@` from `@@LOG@@` and limits old-worker
+shutdown to ten seconds. Application, frontend and efsn code are unchanged.
+These files are deployment candidates; local testing does not install a public
+service or select its domain, address, certificates or capacity.
+
+## Provision and render
+
+Provision a dedicated system account and group named `fsn-stats-proxy`, without
+a login shell, home directory or validator keys. This proxy uses a stable account
+so file ownership and logrotate's `su`/`create` identities remain consistent.
+The three application services retain their separate dynamic identities.
+
+Use the reviewed distribution nginx executable at `/usr/sbin/nginx`, or explicitly
+adjust all three executable references in the unit. Do not run the default nginx
+service against this same configuration. The custom unit manages one foreground
+master, using the template's `daemon off`. Its only retained capability is binding
+privileged ports; the rest of the process runs unprivileged with a read-only
+filesystem except its managed runtime and log directories.
+
+Render the [proxy template](proxy-tls.md) with these host paths:
+
+| Field | Candidate host value |
+| --- | --- |
+| `@@RUN@@` | `/run/fsn-stats-proxy` |
+| `@@LOG@@` | `/var/log/fsn-stats-proxy` |
+| `@@BUILD@@` | Reviewed compiled frontend directory, readable by the proxy |
+| `@@CERT@@`, `@@KEY@@` | Protected certificate/key pair selected by the administrator |
+
+Supply the remaining host, port and loopback-upstream values explicitly. The
+template still listens on loopback; public binding is a separate reviewed change.
+Write the rendered file to `/etc/fsn-stats/nginx.conf`, root-owned and mode 0640
+with group `fsn-stats-proxy`. Give that group directory traversal and read access
+to the selected certificate/key files, but no write access. Keep environment
+files and application credentials root-only as described in
+[service supervision](service-supervision.md).
+
+Systemd creates `/run/fsn-stats-proxy` with mode 0700 and the persistent log
+directory with mode 0750. Install the three unit files into `/etc/systemd/system/`.
+Install the root-only logrotate configuration at `/etc/fsn-stats/logrotate.conf`;
+do not also include it in `/etc/logrotate.d`. The custom timer owns this schedule
+and its separate state file at `/var/lib/fsn-stats-logrotate/status`. Install the
+existing `journald@fsn-stats.conf` profile for service startup/reload diagnostics.
+Verify the installed units, reload systemd, then start the proxy and rotation
+timer. Enable boot startup only as part of the selected host's acceptance.
+
+## Recovery and controlled reload
+
+The proxy has the same five-second restart delay and five-starts-per-minute
+limit as the application services. A failed worker is replaced by nginx's
+existing master; a failed master is replaced by systemd. Deliberate service stop
+uses SIGQUIT and stays stopped. The fifteen-second service stop deadline bounds
+remaining processes. Check actual HTTPS/WSS and fresh reports after recovery.
+
+`systemctl reload fsn-stats-proxy` first runs `nginx -t` under the service identity,
+then sends HUP only if validation succeeds. Old workers retire within the
+template's ten-second shutdown budget. Existing WebSocket sessions can close
+and must reconnect; this reload is not a promise of uninterrupted telemetry.
+The local drill observes successful reconnection and fresh reports.
+
+For certificate replacement, provision a complete immutable directory containing
+the new key and certificate chain with the required ownership. Select that pair
+atomically, for example through an administrator-owned `current` symlink, then
+reload. Check a new TLS connection with normal chain and hostname verification
+and confirm the intended certificate is served. A successful HUP command alone
+does not prove activation. Keep the previous pair until acceptance completes.
+
+If validation fails, the tested service keeps serving its already-loaded pair.
+Restore the valid on-disk selection immediately: a subsequent crash/reboot would
+otherwise try to start with the rejected files. Inspect service and nginx error
+logs, repair the candidate and retry. The local test covers a mismatched key,
+restoration and later successful process recovery.
+
+The public CA/ACME client, protected renewal account, authorization method,
+renewal schedule, full-chain/expiry checks, failure alerts and host-specific
+reload hook remain to be selected and rehearsed. Short-lived fixture certificates
+are never deployment material. The
+[nginx reload semantics](https://nginx.org/en/docs/control.html) inform this
+procedure; certificate acceptance is checked independently over TLS.
+
+## Rotation and retention
+
+The timer checks every five minutes. Logrotate requests daily rotation, earlier
+rotation above 8 MiB, at most seven archives per log, seven-day age cleanup,
+compression and one-cycle delayed compression. It renames files and signals the
+manager-owned nginx master to reopen them. It does not copy and truncate an open
+log. New files have mode 0640 and the stable proxy owner/group. Rotation remains
+valid while the proxy is deliberately stopped.
+
+The local drill triggers the real timer/service with a test-only one-second
+schedule and padded fixture logs above 8 MiB. It checks master/worker descriptors
+point at the new inodes, then forces eight additional rotations and verifies
+archive count/content, compression, owner/mode and uninterrupted telemetry.
+It does not wait seven days or measure public traffic capacity.
+
+These settings are not a hard disk quota or seven guaranteed days of history.
+Files can exceed 8 MiB between timer checks, archive count may remove recent
+history sooner, and age cleanup occurs when rotation runs. Provision disk space
+and alerts for growth, rotation errors, failed timers and nginx reopen failures.
+Do not silently ignore a failed postrotate signal. The exact semantics are in
+the [logrotate manual](https://github.com/logrotate/logrotate/blob/3.21.0/logrotate.8.in).
+
+Access logs omit query strings and request bodies. nginx error diagnostics can
+include the request target, including its query. Do not put telemetry credentials
+in URLs; they remain in the existing TLS-protected reporter hello message. Apply
+log access/retention policy to both streams. The local fixture demonstrates this
+difference with non-secret markers.
+
+Inspect the proxy files, `journalctl --namespace=fsn-stats`, the host service-manager
+journal, `systemctl status fsn-stats-proxy fsn-stats-logrotate` and
+`systemctl list-timers fsn-stats-logrotate.timer`. Process state alone is not health.
+Public-host reboot, capacity, sustained retry/log volume and notification delivery
+remain deployment gates.
